    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“You know how to wake dead metal just a little too well.”</em></p><p>When you finish a Soma Break, you may choose one <strong>construct, device, vehicle, or weapon</strong> you repaired, salvaged, or forged during or before the rest.</p><ul><li>For the next <strong>hour</strong>, it gains <strong>+1 to attack rolls</strong> (if it makes attacks) and <strong>+1 to Guard</strong> (if it can be targeted and has a Guard).</li><li>Once per round, the first time it hits or successfully completes a relevant action, it deals an extra <strong>1d8 lightning or sephirotic damage</strong> (your choice when you apply the overcharge).</li><li>If the item or construct is destroyed while overcharged, you immediately reroll the lowest die on your next tool check and salvage action this scene, as the feedback pours a blueprint directly into your hands.</li></ul><p><strong>Domain Echo..</strong> If you successfully reclaim at least one meaningful Material, Component, or marks via salvage during the hour, your Domain gains <strong>+10 Economy marks</strong> for the next turn (once per scenario).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
